{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 299,
    "dDurationMs": 3531,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To make a laser, all you need to do is give\na big collection of atoms enough energy so"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3830,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they're excited and ready to emit light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6310,
    "dDurationMs": 4410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Once one of them spontaneously emits a photon,\nit'll stimulate some of the others to do so,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10720,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you get a nice cascade of illumination."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12850,
    "dDurationMs": 3509,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But instead of letting all the light escape,\nit's more powerful to trap it between two"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16359,
    "dDurationMs": 3461,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mirrors and let it to bounce back and forth\nthrough the atoms."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19820,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All that passing light will stimulate them\nto emit even more light, and as long as you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23500,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "keep on re-exciting the atoms, they're happy\nto go on emitting light forever."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26960,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But why do the atoms emit light just because\nanother photon passes by?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31080,
    "dDurationMs": 1490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's actually pretty simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32570,
    "dDurationMs": 3329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Imagine flipping two coins:\nthey can either be in the same state,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35899,
    "dDurationMs": 1491,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or in different states."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37390,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But photons aren't like coins - no matter\nhow hard you try, you can't tell one apart"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41260,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from another."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42260,
    "dDurationMs": 3439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in a \"photon-flipping\" experiment, that\nmeans there's only one way for them to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45699,
    "dDurationMs": 3601,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in different states, but two ways for them\nto be in the same state."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49300,
    "dDurationMs": 3770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So they're more likely to be in the same state,\nand in general, this implies that photons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53070,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "always want to be like other photons - to\nhave the same phase, polarization, and go"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57530,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the same direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59030,
    "dDurationMs": 3709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what's more amazing is that if a solitary\nphoton passes by an excited atom that could"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62739,
    "dDurationMs": 3331,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "emit another photon, there's a good chance\nit will emit one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66070,
    "dDurationMs": 4610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because the two photons want be together - even\nBEFORE the second one exists."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70680,
    "dDurationMs": 3381,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So once you have all these friendly photons\nbouncing around between the mirrors, you can"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74061,
    "dDurationMs": 4059,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just open up a little hole at the end and\nlet out a blinding stream of coherent light:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78120,
    "dDurationMs": 2450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a laser beam."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80570,
    "dDurationMs": 4330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To see lasers in action, check out this sweet\nepisode of \"Smarter Every Day\" showing a laser"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84900,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can stick your hand inside!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86600,
    "dDurationMs": 1810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They also have a bunch of other cool science\nvideos."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88410,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To see lasers in action, check out this episode\nof showing a laser you can stick your hand"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90420,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inside!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91420,
    "dDurationMs": 790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if you like it, he also has a bunch of\nother cool science videos."
    } ]
  } ]
}
